@startuml
title 4G LTE Attach + Default Bearer Setup (End-to-End Sequence)

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam participantPadding 10
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam maxMessageSize 80

actor UE
participant "eNodeB\n(LTE RAN)" as ENB
participant "MME\n(Control Plane)" as MME
participant "HSS\n(Subscriber DB)" as HSS
participant "SGW\n(User Plane Anchor)" as SGW
participant "PGW\n(Internet GW)" as PGW
participant "PCRF\n(Policy/QoS)" as PCRF
participant "Internet/DN" as DN

== (A) RRC Connection ==
UE -> ENB: RRC Connection Request
ENB -> UE: RRC Connection Setup
UE -> ENB: RRC Connection Setup Complete\n(NAS: Attach Request)

== (B) NAS Attach & Authentication ==
ENB -> MME: S1-AP Initial UE Message\n(NAS Attach Request)
MME -> HSS: Update Location / Auth Info Req (S6a)
HSS --> MME: Auth Vector + Subscription Data

MME -> ENB: NAS Authentication Request
ENB -> UE: NAS Authentication Request
UE -> ENB: NAS Authentication Response
ENB -> MME: NAS Authentication Response

MME -> ENB: NAS Security Mode Command
ENB -> UE: NAS Security Mode Command
UE -> ENB: NAS Security Mode Complete
ENB -> MME: NAS Security Mode Complete

== (C) Default Bearer Setup ==
MME -> SGW: Create Session Request (S11)\n(IMSI, APN, EPS Bearer)
SGW -> PGW: Create Session Request (S5/S8)
PGW -> PCRF: Credit/Policy Request (Gx)
PCRF --> PGW: PCC Rules + QoS

PGW --> SGW: Create Session Response\n(UE IP, TEIDs, QoS)
SGW --> MME: Create Session Response\n(Bearer Context)

MME -> ENB: Initial Context Setup Request\n(Bearer/QoS, TEIDs)
ENB -> ENB: Setup DRB + S1-U tunnel
ENB --> MME: Initial Context Setup Response

== (D) Attach Complete ==
MME -> ENB: NAS Attach Accept\n+ Default Bearer Info
ENB -> UE: NAS Attach Accept
UE -> ENB: NAS Attach Complete
ENB -> MME: NAS Attach Complete

== (E) User Plane Data ==
UE <-> ENB: User Data (LTE Radio)
ENB <-> SGW: S1-U GTP-U Tunnel
SGW <-> PGW: S5/S8 GTP-U Tunnel
PGW <-> DN: SGi IP Traffic

note bottom
NAS is logically UE<->MME but carried via eNB.
Control Plane: S1-MME, S6a, S11
User Plane: S1-U, S5/S8, SGi
end note
@enduml